    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 24th slate with a robust offensive forecast, headlined by **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.12). **Christian Yelich** is our premier play, benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Sugano; the combination of a +13% dynamic platoon advantage and a +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile makes him a mandatory start in the OF1 slot. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone of the lineup with an elite 0.478 xwOBA; despite a middle-of-the-road matchup against Martin, his raw hitting talent and spot in the #2 hole sustain his high efficiency score. For those chasing stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014**Caleb Durbin** (65.95) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) offer significant value, as both leverage soft-tossing matchups to secure positions as top-tier starts.\n\nThe decision to keep **Carson Benge** (55.19) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While his score is respectable, the depth of our outfield and utility spots\u2014specifically the surging **Lars Nootbaar** (63.36)\u2014created a bottleneck. Even with a 41% rain risk clouding **Lars Nootbaar**\u2019s outlook, his platoon-adjusted projection maintains a higher floor than **Carson Benge**\u2019s baseline. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Dillon Dingler** (41.99); while he slots into the #3 hole, his score is suppressed by a negative platoon differential against Way, putting him squarely in the \"marginal\" category. We will monitor the weather in the **Lars Nootbaar** game closely, but for now, the Zebras\u2019 focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to manufacture runs against tough arms like Schlittler and Jones.",
